<title>USA: APICS business outlook index fell to 52.4 in June.</title>
<headline>APICS business outlook index fell to 52.4 in June.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The American Production and Inventory Control Society (APICS) business outlook index fell slightly for the second month in a row, declining to 52.4 in June from 53.0 in May.</p>
<p>The index registered 53.4 in April.  </p>
<p>The current component index slipped to 51.9 in June versus 52.8 the previous month. The future component index declined marginally to 52.9 from 53.2.</p>
<p>A reading of 50 indicates neutral sentiment, APICS said.</p>
<p>&quot;The results of the individual components were mixed,&quot; APICS said.</p>
<p>Both current and planned production were &quot;quite strong,&quot; but shipments and new orders both fell, it said.</p>
<p>The APICS index is compiled monthly from a survey of manufacturing firms and is calculated by averaging respondents' ratings of current and future conditions.  </p>
